[Mission.Objectives]
The British are trying to reach Caen and you must stop them.
[Mission.Description]
British troops, under the command of General Montgomery, intend to seize Villers-Bocage and then push on to Caen. At your disposal are several tanks from the Schwere SS-Panzer-Abteilung 101, including tank ace Michael Wittmann. Strike fast and strike hard against the British armored column heading your way. 

Your orders:
-	 Stop the British armored column. Destroy as many enemy tanks and equipment as possible.  
[Mission.Success]
Mission accomplished! Your actions today will be remembered for years to come.
[Mission.Failed]
Mission failed! An opportunity to inflict serious damage on the British forces was lost.
[Submission_1.Objectives]
Attack the enemy armored column.
[Submission_1.Description]
Elements of the British 7th Armored Division are on road march, heading toward the small town of Villers-Bocage, on their way to Caen. 

Your orders: 
-	Use surprise, speed and your superior tanks to inflict the maximum damage on the British forces.	 
[Submission_1.Success]
You have decimated the British forces.
[Submission_1.Failed]
Your attack has failed.
[Submission_2.Objectives]
Keep Michael Wittmann and his tank crew alive if you can.
[Submission_2.Description]
Tank ace Michael Wittmann and his crew are extremely valuable as a fighting force and a symbol. You must keep him and his crew alive at all costs!
[Submission_2.Success]
Michael Wittmann has survived the battle and will no doubt continue to harass the allied forces in battles to come.
[Submission_2.Failed]
Michael Wittmann has been killed. 
[Submission_3.Objectives]
Continue your attack against the remaining British forces.
[Submission_3.Description]
You have struck fear and destruction upon the British forces. Continue to engage the remaining British forces.

Your orders: 
-	 British forces appear to be reforming around a small farm in this area, find and destroy them.
[Submission_3.Success]
Your attack on the farm has been successful.
[Submission_3.Failed]
Your attack against the British forces around the farm has failed.
[Submission_4.Objectives]
Capture a key strategic location near a small farm.
[Submission_4.Description]
The enemy has been detected around a farm near Villers-Bocage. This farm lies near a strategic crossroads and must be taken.

Your orders: 
-	 Destroy the British units around the farm.
-	 Hold the farm against any British counter-attack.
[Submission_4.Success]
You have captured the farm and routed the British units.
[Submission_4.Failed]
Your attack on the farm has failed.
[Submission_5.Objectives]
Resist all attempts by the British to retake the farm.
[Submission_5.Description]
You have surprised the British troops and dealt them substantial damage but they are beginning to reform and regroup and are determined to take the town of Villers-Bocage. You must fend off this counter-attack.

Your orders:
-	 Beat off the enemy counter-attack.
[Submission_5.Success]
You’ve won! Your actions today will go down forever in the annals of war.
[Submission_5.Failed]
You’ve been defeated and the British push toward Caen will continue unimpeded.
[StringTable.inf_reserv]
An infantry squad has been placed at your disposal.
[StringTable.tank_reserv]
You have issued additional tanks from our reserves.